<%# app/views/faqs/index.html.erb
    Public standalone FAQ page. Content is hardcoded below — add a question by
    copying one <details class="faq-item"> block and editing the text. %>

<style>
  /* ---- Page shell ---- */
  .faqp-header {
    background: #102a4d;
    padding: 48px 24px 44px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .faqp-header h1 {
    font-family: 'Poppins', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 38px);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .faqp-header p {
    font-size: clamp(14px, 2vw, 17px);
    color: #cbd5e1;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .faqp-body {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 24px 48px;
  }
  .faqp-back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0b2b4b;
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .faqp-back:hover { opacity: 0.7; }

  /* ---- Section grouping ---- */
  .faqp-section-title {
    font-family: 'Poppins', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0b2b4b;
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
  }
  .faqp-section-title:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }

  /* ---- Accordion (native <details>, no JS) ---- */
  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .faq-item {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.16s ease, box-shadow 0.16s ease;
  }
  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: #0b2b4b;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 22px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  }
  .faq-item > summary {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 16px 48px 16px 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111827;
    line-height: 1.5;
    position: relative;
  }
  .faq-item > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item > summary::after {
    content: "\f078"; /* chevron-down */
    font-family: "Font Awesome 6 Free", "Font Awesome 5 Free";
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #0b2b4b;
    position: absolute;
    right: 20px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    transition: transform 0.18s ease;
  }
  .faq-item[open] > summary::after {
    transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(180deg);
  }
  .faq-item > summary:hover { background: #f8fafc; }
  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 20px 18px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .faq-answer p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .faq-answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .faq-answer ul, .faq-answer ol {
    margin: 0 0 10px 20px;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .faq-answer li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .faq-answer a { color: #0b2b4b; font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---- Disclaimer ---- */
  .faqp-disclaimer {
    background: #f1f5f9;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    padding: 14px 24px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #64748b;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .faqp-disclaimer a { color: #0b2b4b; }
</style>

<div class="faqp-header">
  <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <p>Answers to common questions about eviction, mediation, and how this platform works.</p>
</div>

<div class="faqp-body">
  <%= link_to root_path, class: "faqp-back" do %>
    <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to home
  <% end %>


  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I have to mediate?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>No. Mediation is voluntary. Everyone involved must agree to participate. You, the other person, or the mediator may end the mediation at any time.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Why should I try mediation?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Mediation gives landlords and tenants a chance to solve problems together. Going to court can take time, cost money, and cause stress. Mediation may help both sides avoid some of the costs of an eviction.</p>

        <p><b>Possible Costs for Landlords</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Total cost:</b> $5,000+</li>
          <li><b>Court filing fees:</b> $128–$165</li>
          <li><b>Attorney fees:</b> About $150</li>
          <li><b>Writ of Restitution (Red Tag):</b> $35</li>
          <li><b>Set-out costs:</b> $45</li>
          <li><b>Cleaning or repairs:</b> About $3,000</li>
          <li><b>Lost rent:</b> varies</li>
          <li><b>Missed work:</b> Time away from work to attend court</li>
          <li><b>Time:</b> An eviction may take several weeks or longer</li>
        </ul>

        <p><b>Possible Costs for Tenants</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Eviction record:</b> An eviction filing may appear in court records and may affect future housing applications.</li>
          <li><b>Past-due rent:</b> You may still owe unpaid rent, property damage costs, or interest.</li>
          <li><b>Transportation:</b> Parking, bus fare, or other costs to get to court.</li>
          <li><b>Missed work:</b> You may lose income from taking time off for court.</li>
          <li><b>Time:</b> Traveling to court and attending hearings takes time.</li>
          <li><b>Stress:</b> Going through an eviction case can be stressful.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Mediation may help landlords and tenants avoid some of these costs by working toward a solution before the dispute goes further.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What happens if we reach an agreement?</summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>You and the other person decide what you agree to. The mediator can help put the agreement in writing so everyone understands what they agreed to do.</p>
        <p>The agreement is <b>not filed with or enforced by the court.</b> Instead, both people are expected to follow through on what they agreed to. The process depends on trust, communication, and accountability from both sides.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What if mediation does not work? </summary>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <p>Mediation does not always end in an agreement. Either person can decide to stop participating. If you cannot reach an agreement, you may still have other options for handling the dispute.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

<div class="faqp-disclaimer">
  <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This page provides general information only and is not legal advice.
  For legal help, please consult a lawyer or visit
  <a href="https://www.ohiolegalhelp.org/guide/housing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ohio Legal Help</a>.
</div>
